                "title": "Chief Technology Officer",
                "description": "As CTO at IP Fabric, I lead the transformation of the Engineering organization into a high-performing, execution-focused team capable of delivering at scale. Since joining, my focus has been on strengthening the fundamentals of how we operate. This includes introducing clearer ownership, improving performance management, and building a culture of accountability, transparency, and continuous improvement.\n\nI redesigned the Engineering structure to separate people and technical leadership, introduced platform teams, and established clearer alignment between Product and Engineering. In parallel, I shifted hiring toward senior talent, strengthened performance evaluation practices, and implemented structured planning processes such as delivery reviews and roadmap discipline. I am also driving adoption of AI across Engineering as a core productivity lever by scaling the use of code-assist tools and embedding them into everyday workflows. Together with introducing structured leadership goals, this has helped create a more focused, aligned, and outcome-driven organization, positioning Engineering to support IP Fabric\u2019s continued growth and long-term ambition.\n\nAlongside internal transformation, I work closely with key customers to deliver more value and manage escalations when they arise. I regularly participate in enterprise client discussions, QBRs, and strategic engagements to ensure strong alignment between product direction, engineering execution, and customer needs.",
